WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.550
REELS:
On March 10, 2023, Meta announced that they

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:09.170
would no longer be offering bonuses to Reels
creators on Instagram or Facebook.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:14.900
This was a massive surprise given that everyone
else was doubling down on short form content

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.580
in order to compete against TikTok.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:21.609
But, Zuckerberg had chosen to go against the
grain and pull back on short form content.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:22.609
Why?

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:26.730
Well, promoting reels was actually losing
Meta quite a bit of revenue.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.869
It turns out that people scrolling through
Reels is a lot less profitable than people

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:36.550
scrolling through the Instagram feed, $500
million less per quarter or $2 billion less

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.810
per year to be precise.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:42.480
Hearing this, you’re probably inclined to
think that Reels were taking a massive toll

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.570
on Instagram’s top line and that’s why
decided to pull back.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:52.340
After all, if this was WhatsApp, that $2 billion
toll would be twice their total annual revenue,

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.390
but the same cannot be said about Instagram.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.940
In fact, it’s actually the exact opposite
with Instagram.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:04.440
In 2023, Instagram is expected to pull in
just over $50 billion in revenue.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.990
Let me put that in perspective.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:12.299
That’s $20 billion more than YouTube, $37
billion more than TikTok, and over 11 times

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:13.830
more than Snapchat.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:19.140
In fact, Instagram is the second most lucrative
social media platform in the world only beaten

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.900
out by Facebook themselves.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.550
So, out of all the players that are pursuing
short form content, Instagram is actually

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:32.170
the most well off, and that $2 billion toll
only translates to 4% of their annual revenue.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:37.430
So, Zuckerberg’s decision to pull back from
shorts is less of a financial move and more

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.160
of a strategic move.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.900
Of course, he’s not gonna remove Results
altogether from the platform and stay completely

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:44.900
out of the loop.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:49.310
But, it’s clear that he would rather continue
to focus on core Instagram products and treat

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.780
Reels as an addition to business instead of
as the future of the business.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:02:00.950
And given how well Instagram is already doing,
this seems like strategic calcluated choice.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.600
But all of this still leaves the question,
how in the world does Instagram make so much

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.870
money off of just pictures?

